<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <RootNamespace>Vixen.App</RootNamespace>
        <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <Description>
            The host an application boots through: VixenApp.Run&lt;TGame&gt;(args) picks a platform,
            opens a window, wires the services and owns the frame loop — and every step of it is a
            documented sequence the application can inline and edit instead.
        </Description>
        <PackageTags>host;bootstrap;game-loop;app;game-engine;vixen</PackageTags>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" Visible="false" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core\Vixen.Core.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.Diagnostics\Vixen.Core.Diagnostics.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.IO\Vixen.Core.IO.csproj" />

        <!--
          The content the application loads. A host that could not open a catalog left every game to
          stand up the catalog, the bundle source and the manager itself, which is what Samples/07
          does by hand and what a game should not have to. Vixen.Assets is runtime-profile and
          AOT-clean — it is already rooted in Tools/Vixen.AotProbe.
        -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Assets\Vixen.Assets.csproj" />

        <!--
          The world, the systems, the behaviours and the fixed-step accumulator. A Game with a world
          is what this host exists for, so it builds one unless AppConfig.UseEngine says otherwise —
          which is what a tool head, a server with its own loop, or a UI-only app head says.

          Note what this is not: it is not a licence for Vixen.Ui to reference Vixen.Engine. That
          boundary is about Vixen.Ui and CheckArchitecture still enforces it.
        -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Engine\Vixen.Engine.csproj" />

        <!--
          The frame. WorldRenderer is the join between a world and a drawn frame — the standard
          features, the shared geometry buffer, the extraction systems and a SceneRenderHost — and
          until this reference existed nothing outside a test project constructed one, so every
          sample built the whole stack by hand and none of them was a game.
        -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Engine.Renderer\Vixen.Engine.Renderer.csproj" />

        <!--
          And the two backends an app head can boot on its own. Doc 02 describes Vixen.App as the
          package that pulls in the graphics backends valid for a RID, and this is that half: Vulkan
          where there is a surface to present to, Null where there is not — which is doc 17's
          dedicated server, running the same frame shape against a device that draws nothing. A head
          that wants another backend hands one to AppBuilder.WithGraphics and neither of these is
          touched.
        -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Platform\Vixen.Graphics.Vulkan\Vixen.Graphics.Vulkan.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Platform\Vixen.Graphics.Null\Vixen.Graphics.Null.csproj" />

        <!-- The action system. Named here rather than taken transitively through Vixen.Engine,
             because PlatformInput is what joins it to Vixen.Platform and that seam is this
             assembly's own — see PlatformInput.cs. -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Input\Vixen.Input.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Vixen.Core.Threading\Vixen.Core.Threading.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Platform\Vixen.Platform\Vixen.Platform.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Platform\Vixen.Platform.Desktop\Vixen.Platform.Desktop.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Platform\Vixen.Platform.Headless\Vixen.Platform.Headless.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Vixen.App.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
